# Valid counterpart to the .pos: an sview receiver sliced from a numeric variable.
# The receiver is an sview, not a darray, ON PURPOSE — stage1 segfaults compiling a
# non-literal START bound on an array/darray, a pre-existing backend bug tracked
# separately. sview is unaffected, so this stays a pure diagnostic-parity fixture.
def f(s: sview, k: i64) -> void:
    t = s[k:2]
    _ = t
